{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeBoundedSeminormalWeight","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeBoundedSeminormalWeight","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeBoundedFullTwist"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.stdTwoBelow3_isJMWeight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.stdTwoBelow3_isJMWeight","kind":"theorem","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeBoundedSeminormalWeight.lean#L110-L130","doc":"**The `dim > 1` Jucys–Murphy weight vector.**\n\nOn the 2-dimensional `(2,1)` representation of `H₃(q)`, `e₀ = (1,0)` is a JM weight vector with\neigenvalues `q^{2c}` for the contents `c = 0, 1, −1` of the standard tableau `[[1,2],[3]]`.\n\nEvery previous witness for this predicate in the corpus was one-dimensional, and necessarily so:\n`stdTwo_no_stable_extension` shows the unbounded presentation admits no irreducible representation\nat all. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.toLinAlgEquiv'_smul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.toLinAlgEquiv'_smul","kind":"theorem","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeBoundedSeminormalWeight.lean#L106-L108","doc":"Acting by a transported matrix is `mulVec`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.stdTwoEnd3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.stdTwoEnd3","kind":"def","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeBoundedSeminormalWeight.lean#L100-L104","doc":"The `(2,1)` representation of `H₃(q)` as endomorphisms of `Fin 2 → K`, where the module\nstructure `IsJMWeightB` needs actually exists. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jmRawB_map","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jmRawB_map","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeBoundedSeminormalWeight.lean#L87-L92","doc":"The JM elements transport too. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.map_σ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.map_σ","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeBoundedSeminormalWeight.lean#L83-L85","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.HeckeGeneratorsBelow.map","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.HeckeGeneratorsBelow.map","kind":"def","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeBoundedSeminormalWeight.lean#L68-L81","doc":"Push a bounded presentation along an algebra equivalence.  Every relation is an equation\nbetween products of generators and `algebraMap`s, all of which an `AlgEquiv` preserves. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.fullTwistB_smul_of_weight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.fullTwistB_smul_of_weight","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeBoundedSeminormalWeight.lean#L58-L64","doc":"**The full twist acts by the product of the eigenvalues.**  The bound `l < n` is the one\n`jmProdB_eq_deltaB_pow` needs. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jmProdB_smul_of_weight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jmProdB_smul_of_weight","kind":"theorem","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeBoundedSeminormalWeight.lean#L46-L56","doc":"The ordered product acts by the product of the eigenvalues. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.IsJMWeightB","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.IsJMWeightB","kind":"def","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeBoundedSeminormalWeight.lean#L41-L44","doc":"**A Jucys–Murphy weight vector** on the bounded presentation: every `Lₖ` with `k < m` acts on\n`v` by a scalar `cₖ`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}